Acceptance Criteria
When a user clicks a download CTA in a Product HEro component, a Link Click event fires with the following payload:



{
event: Link Click,
linkDetails: {
clickName: <button text>,
clickDestination: <destination_url>,
clickLocation: body,
clickType: <autopopulated>
clickContext: <title>,
componentContext: <component name>
}
}
When a user clicks the second CTA in a Product Hero component, a Link Click event fires with the following payload:



{
event: Link Click,
linkDetails: {
clickName: <button text>,
clickDestination: <destination_url>,
clickLocation: body,
clickType: <autopopulated>
clickContext: <title>,
componentContext: <component name>
}
}
When the payload is inspected on any of the above components that fire a Link Click event, the clickName dynamically reflects the actual rendered button or link text — not a hardcoded value.

 clickDestination if there is a value for this field, the destination URL must always be a full URL. If there is a hashed component, please include that, eg https://www.lumen.com/en-us/page.html#products. If there is no value (e.g. a toggle click) this value should be blank.

clickLocation the values for this field will always be header, body or footer - this value should be “body” for all product hero

clickContext DIA + LCV essentials (Identify what offer / card / module that CTA belonged to and provide a friendly name for reporting).

componentContext this value should match the name of the component, for this ticket it should be “product hero”

clickType is auto-populated with the values other, download and exit 

When the event fires a single user interaction (one click), exactly one Link Click event is emitted — no duplicate events on a single click interaction.
